spec: S01-17, S16-04, S18-06, S18-09, S26-01, S26-02, S29-30, S29-31, S37-08, S39-06

The `--json ?` contract of every verb in one place (ticket 16's sweep): each lists every field
its `--json` can carry (`--json a,b` narrows to some of them) and exits 0 without calling the
server — so this runs with profile `down` (an unreachable server) and on any platform (`daemon`
answers `--json ?` before looking at the OS). A verb that gains or renames a field changes this
golden; `serve` has a `--json` only with `--setup-only` (S37-08).

```console
$ annotary -p down list --json ?
id name version action open updated vault by message deleted created

$ annotary -p down push x.md --json ?
name id version same_as already warnings assets threads vault hash url

$ annotary -p down pull x --json ?
md sidecar version name id vault threads assets written

$ annotary -p down show x --json ?
name id vault version by at message action open actions threads same_as deleted url

$ annotary -p down status x --json ?
name id version action open_threads mentions_me seq vault deleted

$ annotary -p down versions x --json ?
number by at message same_as name hash

$ annotary -p down delete x --json ?
name id state vault version

$ annotary -p down restore x --json ?
name id state vault version

$ annotary -p down purge x --json ?
name id state vault version

$ annotary -p down thread list x --json ?
id author anchor body mentions replies resolved deleted created updated version

$ annotary -p down thread show x t1 --json ?
id subject anchor author created body mentions edited_at deleted resolved replies updated

$ annotary -p down thread new x --document -m m --json ?
id subject anchor version created body mentions doc

$ annotary -p down thread reply x t1 -m m --json ?
id thread state version doc

$ annotary -p down thread resolve x t1 --json ?
id thread state version doc

$ annotary -p down thread reopen x t1 --json ?
id thread state version doc

$ annotary -p down thread edit x t1 -m m --json ?
id thread state version doc

$ annotary -p down thread delete x t1 --json ?
id thread state version doc

$ annotary -p down mentions --json ?
doc id thread author anchor body mentions replies created updated version vault

$ annotary -p down wait --json ?
seq kind doc name action version thread comment message excerpt by at type label intent same_as discarded mentions vault

$ annotary -p down rerender x --json ?
